\s2\sb320\sa160\sl-320\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\brdrt\brdrth\brdrw60\brdrcf1 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {\fs28 }{Edit box functions\tcl2}}}
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBOpen{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBOpen}}}\tab Open an edit box{\pard\plain 
\s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Open an edit box (hEBOpen)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID *hEBOpen(INT flags,H_EDIT_BOX *heb);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
VOID *hEBOpen(INT flags,H_EDIT_BOX *heb);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Opens an edit box, as specified by {\cs17\f11\fs16 flags} and by {\cs17\f11\fs16 *heb}.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns the handle of the edit box, if successful, or else {\cs17\f11\fs16 NULL}
 (in which case the user will already have been informed of the failure). The handle should be used to identify this edit box, as opposed to others an application may have, in subsequent {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBxxx} calls.
\par \pard\plain \s21\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \f8\fs20\lang2057 The {\cs17\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX} struct is defined as follows:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 typedef struct\line     \{\line     UWORD maxchars;\line     UWORD vulen;\line     UWORD vislines;\line     P_POINT pos;\line     UWORD win;\line     UWORD font;\line 
    UWORD style;\line     UWORD lead_tot;\line     UWORD lead_top;\line     \} H_EDIT_BOX;
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 It is not necessary for all the fields in this struct to be filled in before a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBOpen}
 is made. Default values are supplied for some of the fields. These defaults are overridden by the supplied values only if corresponding bits are set in {\cs17\f11\fs16 flags}.
\par \pard \widctlpar Possible bits set in {\cs17\f11\fs16 flags} are as follows:
\par \trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx3132\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s34\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f174\fs17\lang2057 {\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX_CLIPBOARD\cell }\pard\plain \s36\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f8\fs20\lang2057 
The edit box is to allocate extra resources so that it can perform the clipboard functions Paste and Copy (with deleted text of size more than one character automatically being cut into the clipboard, as standard for Series 3 editors)\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx3132\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s34\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f174\fs17\lang2057 {\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX_LEFT_CURSOR\cell }\pard\plain \s36\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl 
\f8\fs20\lang2057 A triangular pointing cursor is to be displayed down the left hand side of the edit box, opposite the line with the flashing cursor\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\pard\plain \s34\sa160\sl-220\slmult0
\widctlpar\intbl \f174\fs17\lang2057 {\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX_FONT\cell }\pard\plain \s36\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f8\fs20\lang2057 The font and font style for the edit box are to be as specified in the fields {\cs17\f11\fs16 font} and {
\cs17\f11\fs16 style} in {\cs17\f11\fs16 *heb} (the defaults are the system font with normal style); possible values might be {\cs17\f11\fs16 W_FONT_BASE+1} for the bold font, and {\cs17\f11\fs16 G_STY_ITALIC} for an italic style\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\pard\plain \s34\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f174\fs17\lang2057 {\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX_LEADING\cell }\pard\plain \s36\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f8\fs20\lang2057 The leading
 for the edit box font is to be as specified in the fields {\cs17\f11\fs16 lead_tot} and {\cs17\f11\fs16 lead_top} in {\cs17\f11\fs16 *heb}
 (the defaults being 2 and 1 respectively): the former being the total extra vertical spacing between lines, in addition to the font height, and the latter being how much of the total leading applies at the top of each line.\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx3132\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s34\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f174\fs17\lang2057 {\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX_VISLINES\cell }\pard\plain \s36\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl 
\f8\fs20\lang2057 The edit box is to be {\cs17\f11\fs16 heb->vislines} lines high (the default is one line) - although in all cases, it will scroll vertically if enough text is added to form more lines than can be seen at once.\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 \row \pard \widctlpar The meanings of the remaining fields in the {\cs17\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX} struct, which always have to be filled in by the caller, are as follows:
\par \trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx2052\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 maxchars\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 
The maximum number of characters in total that the edit box can contain (before beeping at the user and displaying a {\cs16\i\f8 Maximum number of characters reached} information message); paragraph ends count as one character each\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx2052\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 vulen\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 
The total visible width of the edit box, in pixels, including any margin required for a left cursor; this width also implicitly defines the wrapping margin for multi-line edit boxes\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\pard\plain 
\s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 win\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 The ID of the enclosing window - which is usually the value {\cs17\f11\fs16 MainWid} returned by a call to {
\cs17\f11\fs16 uFindMainWid}\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx2052\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 pos\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0
\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 The offset of the top left of the edit box, relative to the enclosing window.\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 \row \pard \widctlpar 
The edit box may be further customised, before any keys are passed on to it, by means of many of the calls discussed below.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBHandleKey{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBHandleKey}}}\tab 
Pass a key to an edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Pass a key to an edit box (hEBHandleKey)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBHandleKey(VOID *ebH,INT keycode,INT modifier);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBHandleKey(VOID *ebH,INT keycode,INT modifier);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Delivers the specified keypress to the edit box. This should be either a printable character or an editing key. In practice, {\cs18\scaps\f8 enter} keys should only be allowed through to multi-line editors.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value for an error (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard\plain \s4\sa120\sl-200\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar \b\f5\fs20\lang2057 Formatting in background{\pard\plain \s4\sa120\sl-200\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar \b\v\f5\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {Formatting in background\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Keys which cause a change in the location of line breaks due to word-wrap are treated slightly differently in Hwif editors than in editors used by the built-in applications:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \s23\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f4\fs20\lang2057 
in the built-in applications, only the line containing the cursor is reformatted and redrawn at once, before the edit box checks to see if another keypress is ready to be processed; lines further from the cursor are reformatted and redrawn, if needed, {
\cs16\i\f8 as a background activity} in pauses between the receipt of incoming keys
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}\pard \s23\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}in Hwif editors, any subsequent key is processed only when the edit box has 
been completely reformatted and redrawn.
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 
The difference in performance only becomes apparent for larger editors with longer paragraphs. For programmers wishing to increase the responsiveness of their editors to incoming keys, the following lines of code may be tried:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 GLREF_D UWORD _ebControlFormat;\line \line _ebControlFormat=TRUE;
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 In this case, Hwif editors will, for any one call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBHandleKey}, only reformat and redraw one line (except on receipt of a cursor key). This means it is the responsibility of the program
mer to make a later call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBCompleteFormat} (discussed below) at a suitable moment - for example, when a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 uKeyPressOutstanding} next returns {\cs17\f11\fs16 FALSE}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBCompleteFormat{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBCompleteFormat}}}\tab 
Complete edit box formatting{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Complete edit box formatting (hEBCompleteFormat)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBCompleteFormat(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBCompleteFormat(VOID *ebH);
\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Ensures that the specified edit box is completely formatted and completely drawn. Does nothing if the formatting is already up to date.
\par \pard \widctlpar Only needs to be called explicitly by an application if the static variable {\cs17\f11\fs16 _ebControlFormat} has been set {\cs17\f11\fs16 TRUE} (see above).
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if there was insufficient memory to complete formatting.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseText{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseText}}}\tab 
Sense the text in an edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Sense the text in an edit box (hEBSenseText)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 TEXT *hEBSenseText(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{TEXT *hEBSenseText(VOID *ebH);\tcf
102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Returns a pointer to the buffer where the edit box is currently keeping its own copy of its text.
\par \pard \widctlpar This copy is always zero terminated, so its length can be obtained by a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 p_slen}.
\par The buffer may contain embedded {\cs17\f11\fs16 \\n}'s, representing paragraph ends.
\par \pard \widctlpar Note that the location of the buffer may change as more text is added into the edit box, so there is no point in an application trying to keep a permanent copy of this address.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSetText{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSetText}}}\tab 
Set the text in an edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set the text in an edit box (hEBSetText)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSetText(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBSetText(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Sets the {\cs17\f11\fs16 blen} characters at {\cs17\f11\fs16 *pb} as the text for the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBEmphasise{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBEmphasise}}}\tab Emphasise an edit box
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Emphasise an edit box (hEBEmphasise)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID hEBEmphasise(VOID *ebH,INT flag);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
VOID hEBEmphasise(VOID *ebH,INT flag);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Either emphasises or de-emphasises the specified edit box, depending on the value of {\cs17\f11\fs16 flag} ({\cs17\f11\fs16 TRUE} to emphasise it, {\cs17\f11\fs16 FALSE} to de-emphasise it).
\par \pard\plain \s21\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar \f8\fs20\lang2057 An emphasised edit box displays:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}\pard\plain \s23\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\f4\fs20\lang2057 
a flashing text cursor (unless the width of the text cursor has been set to zero)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}\pard \s23\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}a triangular cursor in the left margin (if the flag {\cs17\f11\fs16 
H_EDIT_BOX_LEFT_CURSOR} was set on initialisation)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs20\lang2057 \'b7\tab}\pard \s23\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\tx720{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\pnf1\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}a highlight between the cursor and anchor points of any select region.
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 A de-emphasised edit box displays none of these features.
\par \pard \widctlpar By default, an edit box is de-emphasised.
\par \pard \widctlpar Applications may wish to surround edit boxes with curved borders, with varying degree
s of shadowing to help indicate whether or not each edit box is currently emphasised. In this case, the application has the responsibility for drawing the borders (using the Wlib call {\cs17\f11\fs16 gBorderRect}).
\par \pard\plain \s4\sa120\sl-200\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar \b\f5\fs20\lang2057 When edit boxes lose their cursor{\pard\plain \s4\sa120\sl-200\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar \b\v\f5\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {When edit boxes lose their cursor\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Note that edit boxes maintain their own record of whether they are emphasised, {\cs16\i\f8 and do nothing} if they receive an {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBEmphasise}
 call instructing them to change their emphasis state to what it already is. Thus in the following sequence of code
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 hEBEmphasise(ebH,TRUE);\line ...\line hEBEmphasise(ebH,TRUE);
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 the later {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBEmphasise} call is ignored, unless a call {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBEmphasise(ebH,FALSE)} has been made in the meantime.
\par \pard \widctlpar The significance of this is as follows: suppose that, in the meantime, a flashing text cursor is drawn elsewhere on the screen by the application. This may be as a result of an explicit call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 wDrawTextCursor}
; more likely, it will be as a side effect of a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 uRunDialog} or {\cs17\f11\fs16 hPrintSetupDialog}. In this case, the text cursor will be removed f
rom the edit box - since there can only be one text cursor per application at any one time. When the intervening text cursor is cancelled - say as the result of the termination of the dialog - it is the responsibility of the application to re-activate the
 flashing cursor where it used to be (if that is still appropriate). However, in the light of what has just been explained, a simple call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBEmphasise} will be insufficient to effect this.
\par \pard \widctlpar Accordingly, applications which contain an edit box as part of their main display, and which invoke dialogs with items which can also display a flashing cursor, need to use a layer of the following sort around calls to {\cs17\f11\fs16 
uRunDialog}:{\*\bkmkstart BM1}
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 LOCAL_C INT RunDialog(VOID)\line     \{\line     INT ret;\line \line     hEBEmphasise(edit[emph],FALSE);\line     ret=uRunDialog();\line     hEBEmphasise(edit[emph],TRUE);\line 
    return(ret);\line     \}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 A similar protective layer is needed around any calls to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hPrintSetupDialog}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\*\bkmkend BM1}hEBSetSelect{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSetSelect}}}\tab 
Set edit box select and cursor{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set edit box select and cursor (hEBSetSelect)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSetSelect(VOID *ebH,INT aoff,INT coff);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBSetSelect(VOID *ebH,INT aoff,INT coff);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Sets the anchor point and cursor point of the specified edit box. Both positions are given as character offsets into the content of the edit box, starting at 0 for the position in front of the first character.
\par \pard \widctlpar Note that neither the anchor point nor the cursor point is permitted to come after the last character in the edit box.
\par To set the cursor position without setting any highlighted select region, pass the value of {\cs17\f11\fs16 aoff} to be equal to that of {\cs17\f11\fs16 coff}.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success or a negative error value (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseSelect{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseSelect}}}\tab 
Sense edit box select and cursor{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Sense edit box select and cursor (hEBSenseSelect)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSenseSelect(VOID *ebH,UWORD *top);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBSenseSelect(VOID *ebH,UWORD *top);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Returns the length of the select region of the specified edit box, and writes the character offset of the top of the select region to {\cs17\f11\fs16 *top}.
\par \pard \widctlpar If there is no select region, the value 0 is returned, and the character offset of the cursor point is written to {\cs17\f11\fs16 *top}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseClipText{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseClipText}}}\tab 
Sense edit box clipboard contents{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Sense edit box clipboard contents (hEBSenseClipText)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 TEXT *hEBSenseClipText(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
TEXT *hEBSenseClipText(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Returns a pointer to the buffer where the clipboard of the edit box is currently keeping its own copy of its text.
\par \pard \widctlpar The form of this buffer is exactly the same as the buffer used for the main text of the edit box (see the discussion on {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSenseText} above).
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSetClipText{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSetClipText}}}\tab 
Set edit box clipboard contents{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set edit box clipboard contents (hEBSetClipText)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSetClipText(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBSetClipText(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Sets the {\cs17\f11\fs16 blen} characters at {\cs17\f11\fs16 *pb} as the text for the clipboard of the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBChangeWidth{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBChangeWidth}}}\tab 
Change width of edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Change width of edit box (hEBChangeWidth)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBChangeWidth(VOID *ebH,INT width);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBChangeWidth(VOID *ebH,INT width);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Changes the width of the specified edit box to {\cs17\f11\fs16 width}. The new width is specified in pixels and includes an allowance for any left margin required to display a left triangular cursor - exactly as for the {
\cs17\f11\fs16 vulen} field of the {\cs17\f11\fs16 H_EDIT_BOX} struct used to initialise the edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar In the case of a multi-line editor, the text is automatically re-formatted, wrapping to the new width. In all cases, the display is scrolled (vertically and/or horizontally) to expose the cursor position.
\par Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par Even if the return value is negative (indicating a failure to re-format the edit box to its new width), the record within the edit box of its width will be updated as requested.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSetCWidth{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSetCWidth}}}\tab 
Set width of edit box cursor{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set width of edit box cursor (hEBSetCWidth)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID hEBSetCWidth(VOID *ebH,INT cwidth);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
VOID hEBSetCWidth(VOID *ebH,INT cwidth);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Changes the width of any flashing cursor displayed. The value of {\cs17\f11\fs16 cwidth} is in pixels.
\par \pard \widctlpar By default, the flashing cursor is two pixels wide.
\par \pard \widctlpar Passing {\cs17\f11\fs16 cwidth} as zero makes the flashing cursor invisible. This may be appropriate when, for example, highlighting some found text by means of the call {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSetSelect}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBInsert{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBInsert}}}\tab 
Insert text buffer into edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Insert text buffer into edit box (hEBInsert)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBInsert(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBInsert(VOID *ebH,TEXT *pb,INT blen);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Inserts the {\cs17\f11\fs16 blen} characters at {\cs17\f11\fs16 *pb} into the edit box at the cursor position. Any select region is cancelled first. The cursor is positioned afterwards to the end of the inserted text.

\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBReplace{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBReplace}}}\tab 
Replace selection in edit box{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Replace selection in edit box (hEBReplace)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBReplace(VOID *ebH,TEXT *replace,INT backwards);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBReplace(VOID *ebH,TEXT *replace,INT backwards);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Deletes any highlighted selection, into the clipboard if the edit box has one, and then inserts the contents of the ZTS {\cs17\f11\fs16 *replace}
 at the cursor position. The cursor is finally positioned at the end of the text inserted, unless {\cs17\f11\fs16 backwards} is {\cs17\f11\fs16 TRUE}, in which case it is placed at the beginning of the selected text.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par The routine was originally designed with the functionality of a Replace command in mind. See also the section below on {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBFind}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBEvaluate{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBEvaluate}}}\tab 
Evaluate edit box expression{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Evaluate edit box expression (hEBEvaluate)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBEvaluate(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBEvaluate(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}}}

\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Attempts to perform the standard Evaluate function on the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par Typical contents of the Evaluate routine called from the {\cs17\f11\fs16 ManageCommand} routine of an application would simply be as follows:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 if (!CheckEditing())          /* check focus is positioned suitably */\line     hEBEvaluate(ebH);         /* ignore any error */
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBCopy{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBCopy}}}\tab Copy function for edit box
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Copy function for edit box (hEBCopy)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBCopy(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBCopy(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Attempts to perform the standard Copy function on the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par But if there is no select region (and hence nothing to copy into the clipboard), the special value 1 is returned.
\par Typical contents of the Copy Text routine called from the {\cs17\f11\fs16 ManageCommand} routine of an application would accordingly be as follows:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 if (!CheckEditing())\line     \{\line     if (hEBCopy(ebH)>0)\line         wInfoMsg("No text to copy");\line     else\line         wInfoMsg("Text copied");\line     \}
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBPaste{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBPaste}}}\tab Paste function for edit box
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Paste function for edit box (hEBPaste)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBPaste(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBPaste(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Attempts to perform the standard Paste function on the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard \widctlpar But if the clipboard is empty (and hence there is nothing to paste), the special value 1 is returned.
\par \pard \widctlpar Typical contents of the Paste routine called from the {\cs17\f11\fs16 ManageCommand} routine of an application would accordingly be as follows:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 if (!CheckEditing())\line     \{\line     if (hEBPaste(ebH)>0)\line         wInfoMsg("No text to insert");\line     \}
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBFind{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBFind}}}\tab Find text within edit box
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Find text within edit box (hEBFind)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBFind(VOID *ebH,TEXT *str,INT flags);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBFind(VOID *ebH,TEXT *str,INT flags);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Attempts to find a copy of the ZTS {\cs17\f11\fs16 *str} in the contents of the specified edit box. If successful, returns {\cs17\f11\fs16 TRUE}
 and automatically creates a highlighted selection over the copy found. Otherwise returns {\cs17\f11\fs16 FALSE} (except if an error occurred, in which case the return value is negative, and the user will already have been notified).
\par \pard \widctlpar The following bits in {\cs17\f11\fs16 flags} determine how the search is done:
\par \trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx2412\cellx9108 \pard\plain \s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 HEB_FIND_BACKWARDS\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 
Search backwards from the cursor position (the default is to search forwards from the cursor position)\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {\f8 \row }\trowd \trgaph108\trleft252 \cellx2412\cellx9108 \pard\plain \s27\sa160\sl-220\slmult0
\widctlpar\intbl \f11\fs16\lang2057 HEB_FIND_CASESENS\cell \pard\plain \s29\sa160\sl-220\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20\lang2057 The search is case sensitive (the default is for a case insensitive search).\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f4\fs20 {
\b\f8 \row }\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBClearChanged{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBClearChanged}}}\tab 
Clear edit box changed flag{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Clear edit box changed flag (hEBClearChanged)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID hEBClearChanged(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{VOID hEBClearChanged(VOID *ebH);
\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Clears the internal "changed" flag of the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar This flag is clear when the edit box is first initialised.
\par \pard \widctlpar This flag is set whenever the contents of the edit box change as a result of any of the calls {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBHandleKey}, {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBInsert}, {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBEvaluate}, {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBPaste}, or {\cs17\f11\fs16 
hEBReplace}.
\par \pard \widctlpar Typically, an application might call {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBClearChanged} following calls to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSetText} or {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSenseText}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseChanged{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseChanged}}}\tab 
Sense if edit box contents have changed{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Sense if edit box contents have changed (hEBSenseChanged)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSenseChanged(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBSenseChanged(VOID *ebH);\tcf
102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Returns the "changed" flag of the specified edit box. See above for some further discussion.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBShowSymbols{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBShowSymbols}}}\tab H
ide or show edit box symbols{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Hide or show edit box symbols (hEBShowSymbols)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBShowSymbols(VOID *ebH,INT flag);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEBShowSymbols(VOID *ebH,INT flag);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Shows or hides end of paragraph symbols and visible space markers, depending on the value of {\cs17\f11\fs16 flag} ({\cs17\f11\fs16 TRUE} to show them, {\cs17\f11\fs16 FALSE} to hide them).
\par \pard \widctlpar These symbols are hidden by default.
\par \pard \widctlpar Returns zero for success, or a negative value if an error occurred (in which case the user will already have been notified).
\par Even if the return value is negative (indicating a failure to re-format the edit box), the record within the edit box of whether to show these symbols will be updated as requested.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBClose{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBClose}}}\tab Close an edit box
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Close an edit box (hEBClose)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID hEBClose(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{VOID hEBClose(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}}}

\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Frees the resources allocated for the specified edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar Any application which uses an edit box throughout its lifetime has no need to close the edit box prior to exiting as any resources used will automatically be fre
ed when the application terminates. However, it may be sensible to close an edit box explicitly if it is only used for a short period during the lifetime of the application. This avoids resources being tied up unnecessarily.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseDoc{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseDoc}}}\tab 
Return handle of edit box document component{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Return handle of edit box document component (hEBSenseDoc)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 VOID *hEBSenseDoc(VOID *ebH);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{VOID *hEBSenseDoc(VOID *ebH);\tcf102}
}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function returns the handle of the document component of an edit box allowing it to be manipulated by other Hwif functions.
\par \pard \widctlpar In some circumstances, the manipulation of the document component rather than the whole edit box can significantly reduce overhead (see {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEDCapacity}, {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEDInsert}, {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBDocChanged}).
\par The parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 ebh} must contain the handle of the opened edit box whose document component is required.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEDCapacity{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEDCapacity}}}\tab 
Set capacity of document component{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set capacity of document component (hEDCapacity)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEDCapacity(VOID *doc,UINT maxlen);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hE
DCapacity(VOID *doc,UINT maxlen);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function sets the capacity of the document component of an edit box. In other words, it specifies the maximum size of the text that the edit box can hold.
\par \pard \widctlpar The parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 doc} must contain the handle of the document component of the edit box as returned from a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSenseDoc}. The maximum size of the text is specified in parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 maxlen}.

\par The function returns zero if successful or a negative value otherwise. If an error occurs, the user will already have been notified.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEDInsert{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEDInsert}}}\tab 
Insert text into document component{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Insert text into document component (hEDInsert)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEDInsert(VOID *doc,UINT pos,VOID *buf,UINT len);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
INT hEDInsert(VOID *doc,UINT pos,VOID *buf,UINT len);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function inserts text into the document component of an edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar The parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 doc} must contain the handle of the document component of the edit box as returned from a call to {\cs17\f11\fs16 hEBSenseDoc}.
\par The text to be inserted is located at {\cs17\f11\fs16 buf} and is {\cs17\f11\fs16 len} bytes long. The text is inserted at offset {\cs17\f11\fs16 pos} within the document component.
\par The function returns zero if successful or a negative value otherwise. If an error occurs, the user will already have been notified.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBDocChanged{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBDocChanged}}}\tab 
Notify edit box that document has changed{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Notify edit box that document has changed (hEBDocChanged)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBDocChanged(VOID *ebh);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBDocChanged(VOID *ebh);\tcf102}
}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 Notifies the edit box that the content of its document component has changed. This causes the text to be re\_formatted.
\par \pard \widctlpar The parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 ebh} must contain the handle of the edit box to be notified.
\par \pard \widctlpar The function returns zero if successful or a negative value otherwise. If an error occurs, the user will already have been notified.
\par Note that no attempt is made to validate the cursor position. It is the programmer's responsibility to set this correctly.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSetMargin{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSetMargin}}}\tab Set word\_wrap margin
{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Set word\_wrap margin (hEBSetMargin)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 INT hEBSetMargin(VOID *ebh,UINT right);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{INT hEBSetMargin(VO
ID *ebh,UINT right);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function allows the right hand word\_wrap margin of an edit box to be set. This value, in effect, sets a limit on the amount of text that can be displayed on one line before being wrapped around onto the next line.

\par \pard \widctlpar The parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 ebh} must contain the handle of the edit box whose margin is to be set. The margin itself is defined by the value in the parameter {\cs17\f11\fs16 right}; this value is measured in pixels.
\par \pard \widctlpar Setting {\cs17\f11\fs16 right} to a large value such as 4096, effectively turns off word\_wrap. In
 fact this is the only sensible use of this function. If there were a need to set a margin smaller than the width of the edit box then it would be easier to use a smaller edit box.
\par \pard \widctlpar The following code fragment suggests how it might be used to turn off word\_wrap:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 H_EDIT_BOX heb;\line VOID *     ebh;\line     ...\line ebh = hEBOpen(H_EDIT_BOX_VISLINES|H_EDIT_BOX_LEFT_CURSOR,&heb);\line hEBSetMargin(ebh,4096);\line     ...
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 The function returns zero if successful or a negative value otherwise. If an error occurs, the user will already have been notified.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBSenseMargin{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBSenseMargin}}}\tab Sense word\_
wrap margin{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Sense word\_wrap margin (hEBSenseMargin)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 UINT hEBSenseMargin(VOID *ebh);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{UINT hEBSenseMargin(VOID *ebh);\tcf
102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function senses and returns the current value of the right hand word\_wrap margin of an edit box whose handle is passed in {\cs17\f11\fs16 ebh}.
\par \pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \shading2000 \b\f5\fs28\lang2057 hEBPosToXL{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\xe {hEBPosToXL}}}\tab 
Convert position to line number and pixel offset{\pard\plain \s3\sb160\sa160\sl-280\slmult0\keepn\widctlpar\tqr\tx8640 \b\v\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\tc {Convert position to line number and pixel offset (hEBPosToXL)\tcl3}}}
\par \pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \f11\fs16\lang2057 UINT hEBPosToXL(VOID *ebh,H_SCRLAY_PLX *plx);{\pard\plain \s22\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\keepn\widctlpar\tx1440 \v\f8\fs20\lang2057 {\tc {\f8\fs20 }{
UINT hEBPosToXL(VOID *ebh,H_SCRLAY_PLX *plx);\tcf102}}}
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 This function converts a character position, within the text of the edit box whose handle is passed in {\cs17\f11\fs16 ebh}, to a position on the screen.
\par \pard \widctlpar The character position is passed in the {\cs17\f11\fs16 pos} member of the {\cs17\f11\fs16 H_SCRLAY_PLX} struct pointed to by {\cs17\f11\fs16 plx}. This struct is defined in {\cs15\i\f8 hwif.h} as:
\par \pard\plain \s26\li360\sa160\sl-200\slmult0\keep\widctlpar \f11\fs16\lang2057 typedef struct\line     \{\line     UWORD pos;\line     WORD line;\line     WORD x;\line     \} H_SCRLAY_PLX;
\par \pard\plain \widctlpar \f4\fs20 If the character position is visible on the screen, the line number and horizontal pixel offset within the line are written to plx\_>line and plx\_>x respectively and the function returns zero.
\par If the character position is above the screen, a value of \_30000 is written to plx\_>line and the function returns \_1.
\par If the character position is below the screen or beyond the end of the text, a value of +30000 is written to plx\_>line and the function returns +1. 
\par }